      },
      "totalDuration": "3 yrs 3 mos",
      "description": "As a Software Engineer, I helped develop the critical Ground based Interval Management system  (GIM-S) for the Time Based Flow Management (TBFM) project. This enhancement introduces ADS-B data into the traffic management system and allows for more accurate spacing of arrivals while the flight is in Center control.",
      "insights": ""
     },
     {
      "title": "Systems Engineer Sr.",
      "timePeriod": {
       "startDate": {
        "month": 4,
        "year": 2012
       },
       "endDate": {
        "month": 6,
        "year": 2013
       }
      },
      "totalDuration": "1 yr 3 mos",
      "description": "I supported the EDSM CSCI of ERAM, once again leveraging my knowledge of Display Command Managment (DCM), as an SE. My primary role is to specify requirements for SW in a way that is understandable, to capture the requirements of our customer (the FAA), and to provide value, safety, and to generally make life easier for Air Traffic Controllers.\n\nIn this role I get to interface with the many CSCIs of ERAM and engineer, at times, complex solutions in the most understandable way possible. This role is broadening my ability to understand the big picture in ATC, as well as allowing my skill set to dig deep into problems that aren't typically within my area of expertise.",
      "insights": ""
     },
     {
      "title": "Software Engineer Sr.",
      "timePeriod": {
       "startDate": {
        "month": 9,
        "year": 2010
       },
       "endDate": {
        "month": 4,
        "year": 2012
       }
      },
      "totalDuration": "1 yr 8 mos",
      "description": "Supported software development in Air Traffic Control for 1.5 years. In particular, I was part of the SW group for Display Command Management. While in this role I delivered SW for PR fixes, PR Engineering Direction changes, and complex requirements updates specified in SIGs. I delivered a Tiger Team PRED, participated actively and constructively in peer reviews and inspections, and implemented a number of process improvement updates for the team.\n\nI was part of the large ICAO 2012 effort to step up command formatting to recent international standards. I received a SPOT award for my efforts.",
      "insights": ""
     }
    ]
   }
